    "summary": "Stellar Dark Star & classic ’70 set despite muddy tape",
    "blurb": "The performance captures a strong early‑’70 vibe with an expansive Dark Star and tight country‑rock numbers. Highlights include Dancin' In The Street, Till the Morning Comes, and a crisp Saint Stephen/Not Fade Away closing run. Recording is muddy but listenable for fans who want this historic set.",
    "review": "On October 11, 1970 at Marion Shea Auditorium the Dead served up an archetypal early‑’70 show that still shines despite the grainy audience tape. The first half rolls through country‑flavored classics—Casey Jones, Till The Morning Comes, Candyman and a soulful Morning Dew—before launching into a wild, wah‑filled Dark Star where Jerry’s tone is described as “ass‑kickin’.” Phil steps forward on Dancin' In The Street with a memorable solo during the “stuck in the mud” section. The set closes with a seamless Saint Stephen → Not Fade Away → Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad → Not Fade Away sequence that caps an otherwise flawless performance. While the recording is muddy and hiss‑laden, it remains listenable for completists who crave this historic New Jersey show.",
